Method:
  1. Ours: encode → drain W44-20 LastPatchesDetectStats thread-local
     (final_unique = ref-frame unique patterns; final_occ = sum of
     PatchPosition::positions.len()).
  2. cjxl: encode → parse main frame's LfGlobal.patches via
     jxl-frame::LfGlobal::<i32>::parse and count
     (patches.len(), sum(patch_targets.len())).
  3. Side-by-side delta.

Hypothesis H1 (W44-52 final): cjxl admits MORE patches via CC
enumeration / patch-admission differences in FindTextLikePatches.
The 7% bigger cjxl ref-frame at d=3-6 could be 1-2 more actual
patches admitted.

Result: H1 RULED OUT. cjxl admits EXACTLY the same 59 unique
patches with 202 occurrences as ours at every distance d=3-6.
delta_unique = 0, delta_occurrences = 0 across all four cells.

Conclusion: codec_wiki patches subsystem is at structural parity
with libjxl. The 4-7% bytes residual is NOT from missing patches
detection or admission. It must come from downstream coding
(ref-frame entropy, AC residual coding, or main-frame headers).

H1-H4 all ruled out for codec_wiki e7 d=3-6:
  - W44-48: is_similar_b / has_similar threshold tuning
  - W44-51: ref-frame predictor (Gradient vs Variable)
  - W44-52: bin-packer canvas layout
  - W44-53: CC enumeration / patch admission

codec_wiki e7 d=3-6 is declared STRUCTURAL CEILING — accepted
residual, similar to F-D family. The 4 OPEN cells in the
cjxl_parity_ledger correspond to coding-side overhead that no
